Derived material:

* `src/tables.rs` is generated programmatically from the data tables in `dcadata.c`, `dcahuff.c`
  and `dcadsp.c`/`dcadata.c` (quantizer step sizes, scale factor tables, ADPCM and high frequency
  VQ code books, joint scale factors, downmix tables, the 32/64-band QMF prototype filters, LFE
  interpolation filters, and the Huffman code book sources), and the fixed-point filter bank
  coefficient tables, the XLL reflection coefficient and frequency band assembly tables.
* `src/tables_dct.rs` is generated programmatically from the fixed-point IMDCT twiddle tables
  computed by `dcadct.c`.
* `src/lbr.rs` is a port of `dca_lbr.c` (DTS Express chunk parsing, scale factor grids, tonal
  components, partial stereo, LPC, hybrid filter bank, IMDCT and LFE IIR); `src/tables_lbr.rs`
  is generated from the LBR tables of `dcadata.c` and `dcahuff.c`.
* `src/xll.rs` is a port of `dca_xll.c` (lossless extension parsing, entropy decoding, inverse
  prediction, decorrelation, frequency band assembly, downmix undo, residual combination with the
  fixed-point core, and peak bit rate smoothing).
* `src/decoder.rs`, `src/exss.rs`, `src/dsp.rs`, `src/huff.rs` and `src/bits.rs` follow the
  bitstream parsing, dequantization, ADPCM, joint intensity, XCH/XXCH/X96/XBR handling,
  extension substream parsing, synthesis filter bank and LFE interpolation logic of the files
  listed above. The synthesis IMDCT is implemented independently as a direct (matrix) evaluation
  of the inverse MDCT definition in the floating-point path; the fixed-point path follows
  `dcadct.c`, `dcadsp.c` and `synth_filter.c` to be bit-exact with the reference.

